Two contract issues remain:

- `go 1.23.4rc1` passes `GoVersionRE`, but Go’s semantic parser rejects prereleases after a patch; Go 1.25.1/1.25.5 panic on the submitted permitted case. See the official [modfile regex](https://go.dev/src/cmd/vendor/golang.org/x/mod/modfile/rule.go) and [Go version parser](https://go.dev/src/internal/gover/gover.go).
- Vector 126 requires comparison coverage to equal all upstream-accepted names, contradicting the intentional rejection of valid custom toolchains such as `go1.21.0-custom` ([official toolchain naming](https://go.dev/doc/toolchain#name)).

All static tests, Go checks, deterministic regeneration, and the rc.5 release gate passed. No project code or candidate artifacts were modified.

